@@ -152,3 +152,17 @@ Validation is staged: public independent CPU/FP64 operations, exact capacities,
 BF16 Add Graph replay, sanitizer, same-GPU inference and fixed-corpus incremental
 PPL. These changes do not establish lossless FP8 or generalize 5060 Ti timings to
 other hardware. The 64 MiB weight image limit is still used at this stage.
+
+## Measured weight-image capacity
+
+The `gguf_prefill_mxfp8/weight-image` device-profile key selects `10.5mib`,
+`16mib`, `32mib` or `64mib`; absent or unknown schedules retain 64 MiB.
+The 36-SM RTX 5060 Ti builtin selects 32 MiB after same-device 256/512/1024
+ordinary/KVMem comparisons and independent CPU/FP64/Graph/memory qualification.
+Other hardware keeps 64 MiB. No automatic image-budget calibration is added.
+The key is part of the serialized numerical/cost profile signature.
+
+The reference's 10.5 MiB candidate reduced sampled card use by 98 MiB at
+chunk1024 but regressed ordinary/KVMem throughput by 3.70%/3.50%; it was rejected.
+The selected budget preserves actual-amax encoding and FP32 gate/up intermediates.
+No BF16 gated intermediate or new weight quantizer is adopted.
